Behavioral reference: Ray Optics Simulation by Rick Tu and contributors
https://github.com/ricktu288/ray-optics/tree/9dd7706097ec8b93171e04e7985be12c3309533c
Version 5.5.0, commit 9dd7706097ec8b93171e04e7985be12c3309533c, Apache License 2.0.

Studied src/core/geometry.js for ray/segment intersections,
src/core/sceneObjs/glass/IdealLens.js for signed ideal-lens bending,
src/core/sceneObjs/mirror/ArcMirror.js for the signed paraxial R/2 focal
distance, src/core/sceneObjs/glass/Glass.js for boundary refraction and
wavelength-dependent index, and src/core/PrimitiveBasedSimulator.js for
the per-ray interaction-depth limit.

The plugin reimplements these ideas with Rust vector geometry, nearest-face
tracing, Snell transmission and total internal reflection, and a bounded
prism trace per wavelength. The principal-ray construction and animation,
labels, rendering and approximate spectral palette are written for AniMathIO.
The formulas for conjugate distances, refraction and Cauchy dispersion are
textbook material. No upstream JavaScript, GPU code, scenes or assets are
copied. The Apache license text is retained in assets/ray-optics-LICENSE
and packaged as licenses/ray-optics-LICENSE.

The component uses wit-bindgen 0.40.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) for AniMathIO ABI
bindings. Resolved Rust dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock.
